Chapter: GopWebChildHeap
  cites Works chapter GopWeb

 The service in a spawned process with the DEFAULT spawn heap, pinned to
 core 0 under a parent that yields so the child actually runs. The
 reading is whether the child is still alive after the hold: a listen
 transport that reserves more than the child's slot kills the child at
 its first allocation, and the guest with it, so the sabotage (raise the
 serve buffer cap past the spawn slot) truncates this output before the
 verdict line rather than turning it False.

Section: Body

  spin : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spin (n) (acc) = if n == 0 then acc else spin (n - 1) (acc + 1)

  hold-yielding : Integer -> Integer
  hold-yielding (rounds) =
    if rounds <= 0 then 0
    else let y = process-yield
    in let s = spin 10000000 0
    in if s < 0 then 0 else hold-yielding (rounds - 1)

  opening : [Console, Concurrent, Capability, Network.Read, Network.Write] Nothing = act
    let blk = gopweb-blk-new
    in act
    svc <- process-spawn-on-core (\x -> gopweb-service blk x) 0
    print-line-uni ("spawned " & show (svc > 0))
    let held = hold-yielding 200
    in act
      print-line-uni ("service alive " & show (process-status svc > 0))
      k <- process-kill svc
      print-line-uni ("service stopped " & show (k >= 0))
    end
  end
